{"author":{"id":"89da5fec8eff6d69dbcdd68f81be7e9163b16f34b17e978ecf3554487379f453"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1774044846,"nonce":"WDENYPVdnjO9UpdcrZB30o8KOE8=","message":"**SpawnBackend clarification**\n\nThe current PTY backend runs TWO processes per session:\n1. Interactive PTY (node-pty): terminal emulation, RingBuffer, WebSocket xterm.js — the \"Debug Terminal\" tab\n2. Spawn child (child_process.spawn): `--output-format stream-json`, JSON stdout parsing — the rich view\n\nSpawnBackend = just #2, without #1. Drop node-pty, drop terminal emulation, drop the dual-process architecture. One child process, JSON stdout parsing, everything renders through StreamRenderer (the rich view).\n\nUser-visible difference: lose the \"Debug Terminal\" tab for Codex/Gemini sessions. The rich view (which is what users actually look at) stays identical.\n\nFor Claude: SpawnBackend is irrelevant — SDK backend already gives typed events + hooks + permissions. SpawnBackend is only for non-Claude agents where no SDK exists.","files":null}]}